### VictoriaMetrics vs Grafana Mimir (self-hosted, one instance per billing-account / region)

| Dimension                                                    | **VictoriaMetrics Cluster**                                                                                                                                                  | **Grafana Mimir**                                                                                                                                                                         |
| ------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Up-stream pedigree & licence**                             | Single-vendor OSS (Apache 2.0). Core ≈35 regular contributors.                                                                                                               | CNCF *incubating* (fork of Cortex); larger community; AGPL v3.                                                                                                                            |
| **Logical architecture**                                     | 3 processes: **vminsert → vmstorage → vmselect** (can run all-in-one). State kept on `vmstorage` (local or network PVC).                                                     | 8–10 micro-services (distributor, ingester, querier, store-gateway, ruler, alertmanager, compactor…). All rely on **object storage** (GCS/S3) for chunks. ([docs.victoriametrics.com][1]) |
| **Resource footprint (benchmark, 10 M active series)**       | \~35 % less CPU & 40 % less RAM than Mimir on identical hardware. Read latency \~30 % lower in Victoriametrics’ public test. ([victoriametrics.com][2], [slideshare.net][3]) | Higher CPU/ RAM but scales linearly with shards; object storage off-loads local disks.                                                                                                    |
| **Operational complexity**                                   | Fewer pods (3 – 9). **StatefulSet** for `vmstorage` makes scale-down trickier; need WAL backups.                                                                             | More helm charts to wire, but all stateless; scaling knobs well documented; easy to add/retire ingesters.                                                                                 |
| **Multi-tenancy / RBAC**                                     | Native *tenantID* label; per-tenant retention via relabel; Grafana datasource plugin supports per-token isolation. ([grafana.com][4])                                        | Built-in multi-tenant auth header + per-tenant object-storage buckets; mature token/tenant CLI.                                                                                           |
| **Data locality & regulator fit**                            | Keep one cluster *per billing project* → data never leaves region; replicate via vminsert if you still want global dashboards.                                               | Same pattern—each project hosts its own Mimir stack writing to regional GCS bucket.                                                                                                       |
| **Grafana dashboarding**                                     | Official **VictoriaMetrics datasource** with automatic query hints.                                                                                                          | Uses standard Prometheus datasource (Grafana authors Mimir).                                                                                                                              |
| **Long-term retention cost**                                 | SSD / regional-PD if hot queries → higher €/GB; can tier to GCS via remote-storage exporter.                                                                                 | Designed for **object-storage first**; cheapest €/GB for >90-day retention.                                                                                                               |
| **High-cardinality label handling** (`tenant_id`, `slot_id`) | Index in memory; practical soft limit ≈150 M series per cluster before RAM pressure.                                                                                         | Index in Bigtable-style KV inside object store; can handle 500 M+ series with compactor.                                                                                                  |
| **Alerting & ruling**                                        | Integrated `vmalert` + `vmalertmanager`.                                                                                                                                     | Compatible with Prometheus Alertmanager; separate `ruler` micro-service.                                                                                                                  |
| **Egress / remote-write**                                    | Accepts Prom RW & OpenTelemetry metrics; automatic relabel pipeline.                                                                                                         | Same; plus exemplar & metadata support identical to Prom.                                                                                                                                 |
| **Learning curve / docs**                                    | Simpler, single set of docs; fewer CRDs.                                                                                                                                     | Heavier doc set but lots of Grafana Labs blogs, reference k8s jsonnet mixins.                                                                                                             |
| **Notable adopters (2024-25)**                               | Prezi, Cloudflare Workers Observability, several EU banks. ([engineering.prezi.com][5])                                                                                      | Unity (migrated from Thanos), GitLab SaaS metrics, many CNCF end-users. ([youtube.com][6])                                                                                                |

